      "created_at": "2020-07-16T03:50:32Z",
      "updated_at": "2020-07-16T03:55:22Z",
      "body": "@rocketsroger Please take a look at this issue. Fenix is currently opening the webpages in the respective apps even if the webpages are opened in the Private Browsing Mode. I think this behavior is a serious breach of user privacy preferences and the Private Browsing Mode itself.\r\n\r\nI think the webpages shouldn't open in app even if the \"Open links in app\" is enabled and only let the users open only if they want through 3-dot menu. What do you think?\r\n\r\nOf course, if the link _has_ to be opened in the app and then it should prompt in that case.\r\n \r\nThanks. :)",
